<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balochistan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Baluchistan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balochistan is an arid, mountainous region on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a>, divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch-people">Baloch people</a>. It lies between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley and the Iranian heartland and has long been a route for armies and trade. Pakistan's province of Balochistan is its largest by area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balochistan.jpg" alt="Balochistan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JohnGold6000 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balochistan_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
